Figure 5 demonstrates that Nano-11 effectively facilitates the transport and uptake of antigens to draining lymph nodes. On both Day 1 and Day 2 post-injection, mice receiving ovalbumin (OVA) formulated with Nano-11 showed a significantly higher mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) of OVA in antigen-containing myeloid cells compared to soluble OVA or OVA with aluminum hydroxide. Nano-11 also increased the percentage of migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) among OVA-positive cells, indicating its specific targeting to these immunopotentiating cells. This evidence supports Nano-11's role in enhancing antigen delivery to critical immune sites for an effective adaptive response.